rk requests.\n3. `--truth` is not checked against the manifest-bound truth path and SHA, permitting alternate repo-local expected values.\n4. Reconstruction authenticates response bytes but evaluates the separately stored `raw_candidate` without reparsing and equality-checking it against those bytes.\n5. Targeted summaries compare 10 current rows against the full 108-row baseline, producing non-like-for-like before/after metrics.\n6. Runner provenance does not bind the imported execution dependencies that directly control parsing, evaluation, checkpoint handling, and serialization.\n7. Provider exhaustion is double-counted as a normalization failure instead of remaining a distinct terminal provider-failure category.\n\nVerification: all 83 offline tests passed with the declared Python dependencies; Python compilation passed; all added JSON parsed with `jq`; `git diff --check` passed. I also reproduced finding 1 through the default `reconstruct` CLI. The current tests cover the successful reconstruction path but do not exercise these failure/provenance cases.\n\nBecause this PR is authored under the same GitHub account, this is a SHA-bound comment review rather than a formal request-changes review.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1634#pullrequestreview-4733596381","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1634","author_association":"OWNER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1634#pullrequestreview-4733596381"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1634"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-20T09:16:21Z","commit_id":"9574473d7e444899cac82154f6b86efb67faf9e4"},{"id":4733646698,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOO5D6p88AAAABGiW3ag","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sams